"How does water get from the sea into the sky?": "69449afa9935",
"It is hot and humid before a storm.": "3a62c6fb4d7d",
"Rain seems simple: water falls from the sky. But how did the water get up there? The sky has no pipes and no tanks. The answer is that the water rose by itself, as a gas that you cannot see.": "81d0757d9a43",
"Rain seems simple: water falls from the sky. But how did the water get up there? The sky has no pipes and no tanks. The answer is that the water rose by itself, as a gas that you cannot see. When the sun warms the sea, some of the water turns into water vapor and mixes with the air. Most of the water vapor in the air comes from the oceans. There is never very much of it, only about one part in a hundred on average, but it makes almost all of our weather. Warm air can hold more water vapor than cold air. If air gets about 11 degrees warmer, it can hold about twice as much. This also works the other way. When air cools, it can hold less, and at a certain temperature it is full. That temperature is called the dew point. So the secret of rain is rising air. Air cools as it rises, about 6.5 degrees for every kilometer. When it has cooled to its dew point, the extra water vapor turns into tiny drops of liquid water. A cloud is a huge crowd of these tiny drops. Inside the cloud the drops bump together and grow, and when they are too heavy to float, they fall. What makes air rise? A mountain is one answer. When moist wind from the sea meets a mountain, the air has nowhere to go but up. Clouds form on that side, the windward side, and the rain falls there. By the time the air crosses the top, it has lost much of its water. It sinks down the other side dry and warm. Taiwan shows this very well. A high wall of mountains runs down the island, and the wind changes with the seasons. In winter the northeast wind brings steady rain to the northeast, while the center and south are mostly sunny. In summer the wind turns, and the south gets most of its rain. The same mountains, the same sea: only the wind has changed.": "637a30c28926",
